35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The eastern avenue planting failed because aftercare was excluded. We repeat this mistake.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,Only two firms can handle the clay subsoil. They flag slippage risk.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The habitat fund only pays for planting and water, not surfacing. That is a trap.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,We have seven staff left. Specialist care is bought in. It is unsustainable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,People cross on firm ground. The drainage callouts have doubled.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, if the fund excludes surfacing, we are stuck with high maintenance.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, the slippage risk means we cannot do heavy earthworks in the center.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The ledger shows planted ground costs triple to maintain.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the volunteer groups are helpful, but they cannot replace professional turf care.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Misaki, the phasing notes say the center cannot be hoarded. That limits options.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The wetland plan fits the fund terms but ignores the staffing reality.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"The woodland plan is risky given the soil, but the paths are simple.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,The market plaza is expensive to maintain and not covered by the habitat fund.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The sports terraces require constant upkeep we do not have.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,The wetland plan addresses the drainage issue directly.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I am leaning towards the wetland plan, despite the risks.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I am concerned about the construction, but the wetland plan is viable.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I am worried about the cost, but the fund terms force our hand.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I am worried about the staffing, but the volunteers might help with observation.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,The wetland plan aligns with the actual usage and drainage needs.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
